WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.280
Imagine you're looking at an x-ray of a patient.

00:03.800 --> 00:07.920
You expect to see the crisp, jagged white line of a broken bone, right?

00:08.000 --> 00:10.240
It's binary. Broken or not broken.

00:10.260 --> 00:11.980
Right, it's a very straightforward diagnosis.

00:12.240 --> 00:12.520
Exactly.

00:13.100 --> 00:17.200
But imagine instead, the x-ray shows the bones moving backward in time.

00:17.620 --> 00:20.820
And the diagnostic machine spits out this mathematical formula,

00:20.980 --> 00:24.820
stating the patient has a negative 20% chance of even existing.

00:25.060 --> 00:26.440
Which is a complete logical paradox.

00:26.440 --> 00:31.720
Yeah. Today's deep dive is about what happens when physics hits exactly that kind of wall.

00:32.080 --> 00:36.400
We're unpacking a massive, just incredibly dense stack of monographs

00:36.400 --> 00:41.020
from an independent researcher named Flyxion, published in mid-2026.

00:41.240 --> 00:46.200
And this work, I mean, it's attempting to outline a radical new unified theory of reality.

00:47.000 --> 00:50.320
We're looking at papers with titles like Adjunction and Irreversibility,

00:50.580 --> 00:54.060
Fossil Manifolds, and Admissibility Interface Extended.

00:54.200 --> 00:55.200
It's heavy stuff.

00:55.200 --> 00:57.100
It really is a remarkable collection of work.

00:57.160 --> 00:59.960
And what we're going to do today is take some of the most complex,

01:00.560 --> 01:03.580
counterintuitive mathematical concepts in modern science.

01:03.680 --> 01:07.140
Stuff that actively challenges our basic assumptions about the universe.

01:07.720 --> 01:08.160
Precisely.

01:08.380 --> 01:12.380
And we're going to translate them into a framework that you can actually visualize and understand.

01:12.720 --> 01:17.060
I mean, we are going to completely redefine time, gravity, quantum mechanics,

01:17.060 --> 01:21.360
and how we actually observe the earliest galaxies in the cosmos.

01:21.360 --> 01:24.840
And if you're listening to this right now and thinking, you know, this sounds completely

01:24.840 --> 01:26.180
unprovable, this sounds insane.

01:26.300 --> 01:28.720
Well, you are exactly where the scientific community was.

01:28.980 --> 01:31.700
Yeah, the initial reaction was highly skeptical.

01:32.040 --> 01:34.820
Because, I mean, how do you prove a mathematical ghost?

01:35.000 --> 01:37.040
How do you observe a universe that moves backward?

01:37.700 --> 01:43.620
But if you've ever felt overwhelmed by how physics, your own cognition, and the society you live in

01:43.620 --> 01:46.700
seem to operate on totally different contradictory rules,

01:46.700 --> 01:51.040
this deep dive is going to show you a hidden architecture connecting them all.

01:51.300 --> 01:52.800
It really is a unifying framework.

01:53.080 --> 01:54.480
So we have a ton of ground to cover.

01:54.760 --> 02:00.100
We are going to start at the absolute foundation, a concept Flyxion calls the RSVP framework.

02:00.700 --> 02:02.540
This is proposed as the substrate of everything.

02:02.940 --> 02:07.640
So what exactly is the relativistic scalar vector plenum?

02:07.640 --> 02:11.920
Let's break that down because it really is the stage upon which this entire theory plays out.

02:11.920 --> 02:16.720
So the RSVP plenum is proposed as a continuous medium.

02:17.760 --> 02:22.040
And in physics, to define a medium, you first need a space to put it in.

02:22.580 --> 02:23.860
Right, a container of some sort.

02:23.960 --> 02:24.260
Exactly.

02:24.980 --> 02:30.800
Flyxion defines this on what is known mathematically as a preferred 3 plus 1 foliation.

02:31.140 --> 02:32.220
Wait, let me stop you right there.

02:32.280 --> 02:35.500
A 3 plus 1 foliation, like slicing space and time.

02:35.500 --> 02:43.080
I'm picturing a loaf of bread where the whole loaf is the universe and each slice is just a single moment in time.

02:43.420 --> 02:45.700
That is actually a very helpful starting point.

02:45.700 --> 02:50.760
Because in Einstein's relativity, the universe is a four-dimensional block, you know, space-time.

02:51.440 --> 02:55.240
Normally, relativity tells us there is no preferred way to slice that loaf.

02:55.380 --> 02:57.340
Because time is relative to the observer.

02:57.560 --> 02:57.900
Exactly.

02:58.480 --> 03:02.520
Depending on how fast you're moving, your slices will cut through the loaf at totally different angles.

03:02.520 --> 03:05.440
But Flyxion's math requires a preferred foliation.

03:06.020 --> 03:12.100
It establishes a specific, universal background slicing of three spatial dimensions evolving over one dimension of time.

03:12.340 --> 03:13.760
Okay, so we have our slices of bread.

03:14.080 --> 03:14.320
Right.

03:14.520 --> 03:18.680
And the plenum, the actual substance of reality, exists within those slices.

03:19.320 --> 03:23.900
But instead of just viewing it as empty space curving under the weight of stars and planets,

03:24.400 --> 03:30.520
the plenum consists of three tightly coupled fields that exist everywhere at all times.

03:30.520 --> 03:34.020
Okay, so reality is literally filled with three fields.

03:34.280 --> 03:34.940
What are they?

03:35.060 --> 03:36.360
First, you have the Greek letter phi.

03:37.040 --> 03:39.100
This represents the scalar potential.

03:39.880 --> 03:41.880
In physical terms, think of it as mass density.

03:42.240 --> 03:45.020
Just how much stuff is at a specific point.

03:45.160 --> 03:49.600
And I noticed in my notes, in cognitive terms, the paper actually refers to this as meaning density.

03:49.940 --> 03:52.440
Yes, we will definitely get to the cognitive mapping later.

03:52.520 --> 03:56.040
But yeah, it's the concentration of significance, or mass.

03:56.380 --> 03:59.020
Now, the second field is the lowercase v, the vector flow.

03:59.020 --> 04:01.560
A vector has both a magnitude and a direction.

04:02.000 --> 04:02.380
Like an arrow.

04:02.660 --> 04:03.600
Exactly like an arrow.

04:03.700 --> 04:05.180
So this represents directional velocity.

04:05.860 --> 04:08.020
It is the literal directed movement of the system.

04:08.140 --> 04:10.980
It's not just that stuff exists, it's that the stuff has a trajectory.

04:11.320 --> 04:13.980
And finally, you have S, the entropy field.

