Human social institutions are modeled as bounding spheres in this fluid.

09:40.420 --> 09:44.760
The scalar potential is the institution's core meaning or ideological mass.

09:44.760 --> 09:48.700
The vector flow is its institutional drive or trajectory.

09:49.800 --> 09:54.000
And the entropy is the institutional friction, like the bureaucratic ritual cost.

09:54.460 --> 09:57.920
So dealing with red tape is literally societal entropy.

09:58.360 --> 09:58.640
Exactly.

09:58.980 --> 10:06.700
Two institutions, say, two corporations or two governments, only merge if the thermodynamic pressure between them overcomes their boundary resistance.

10:06.960 --> 10:08.520
It is unification by substrate.

10:08.920 --> 10:10.440
Not just analogy, but substrate.

10:10.440 --> 10:17.440
Which leads to what might be the most terrifyingly beautiful concept in this whole first section, the unified failure modes.

10:17.760 --> 10:23.520
Because if the math is identical across all these systems, the way these systems die must also be identical, right?

10:23.600 --> 10:25.300
That is the inescapable conclusion.

10:25.840 --> 10:29.280
The theorem states that in what Flyxion terms the Lamford dying regime.

10:29.280 --> 10:30.340
Which is what, exactly?

10:30.480 --> 10:35.200
It's essentially the state where the injection of order or nigentropy into the system completely stops.

10:35.560 --> 10:39.480
When that happens, both the scalar and vector gradients decay exponentially to zero.

10:39.820 --> 10:41.280
